{"v": 1, "key": "cu-cu05", "cards": [{"id": "u3.t.mutualism", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">MU<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tu<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">al<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ism<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"mutualism\" data-audio=\"audio/mutualism.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: mutualism\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"mutualism\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Gut bacteria<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"8.834586466165414\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">get food and a home<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">You<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">get vitamins and<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">protection<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A relationship in which both species benefit.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>互利共生<\/b>：双方物种都受益的关系。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">mutual = both sides gain.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">mutual = 双方都得益。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Name an example of mutualism.<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Gut bacteria and humans, or nitrogen-fixing bacteria and legume roots.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.microbiome", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">MI<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">cro<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">bi<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ome<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"microbiome\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: microbiome\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"microbiome\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"48\" class=\"f1\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"50\" r=\"3\" class=\"f3\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"45\" r=\"3\" class=\"f4\"/><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"65\" r=\"3\" class=\"f3\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"70\" r=\"3\" class=\"f6\"/><circle cx=\"85\" cy=\"78\" r=\"3\" class=\"f4\"/><circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"58\" r=\"3\" class=\"f5\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"8.571428571428571\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">trillions of microbes live in and on you<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">The community of microbes that live on and inside a body.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>微生物组<\/b>：生活在身体表面和体内的微生物群落。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">micro = small, -ome = whole collection.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">-ome = 全部的集合。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Where is the largest part of your microbiome found?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">In the gut (intestines).<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.extremophile", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">ex<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">TREM<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">phile<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"extremophile\" data-audio=\"audio/extremophile.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: extremophile\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u3-extremophile.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"511\" alt=\"Grand Prismatic Spring, Yellowstone, from the air. The orange and yellow rings are mats of microbes living in hot water.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Grand Prismatic Spring, Yellowstone, from the air. The orange and yellow rings are mats of microbes living in hot water.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">从空中看美国黄石公园的大棱镜泉。橙色和黄色的环是生活在热水里的微生物垫。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Jim Peaco, National Park Service · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_prismatic_spring.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"extremophile\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"22\" width=\"90\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Lives in<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">hot springs, salt<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">lakes, acid pools,<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">ice<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"22\" width=\"90\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Loves<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">conditions that<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">would kill most<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">life<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">An organism, often an archaeon, that thrives in extreme conditions such as heat, salt or acid.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>极端微生物<\/b>：在高温、高盐或强酸等极端环境中茁壮生长的生物，常为古菌。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">extreme + -phile (lover).<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">extreme + -phile（爱好者）。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does the ending -phile mean?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Lover of.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.halophile", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">HAL<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">phile<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"halophile\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: halophile\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u3-halophile.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"498\" alt=\"A salt evaporation pond. The pink colour comes from salt-loving microbes that thrive in very salty water.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A salt evaporation pond. The pink colour comes from salt-loving microbes that thrive in very salty water.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">晒盐池。粉红色来自在极咸的水里大量繁殖的嗜盐微生物。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Anfecaro · <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manaure_salt_evaporation_pond.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"halophile\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"15\" y=\"60\" width=\"170\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f1\"/><line x1=\"15\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"185\" y2=\"60\" class=\"\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"80\" r=\"3\" class=\"f6\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"85\" r=\"3\" class=\"f6\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"75\" r=\"3\" class=\"f6\"/><circle cx=\"165\" cy=\"88\" r=\"3\" class=\"f6\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">salt lake<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">halo = salt<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">An organism that lives in very salty places.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>嗜盐菌<\/b>：生活在高盐环境中的生物。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">halo = salt, -phile = lover.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">halo = 盐。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does a halophile love?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Salt.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.thermophile", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">THER<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">mo<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">phile<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"thermophile\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: thermophile\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u3-thermophile.webp\" width=\"533\" height=\"800\" alt=\"Morning Glory Pool, Yellowstone. The green and orange colours come from heat-loving microbes at the edge of the hot water.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Morning Glory Pool, Yellowstone. The green and orange colours come from heat-loving microbes at the edge of the hot water.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">黄石公园的牵牛花池。绿色和橙色来自热水边缘的嗜热微生物。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Dirtsc · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY-SA 3.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Morning_Glory_Pool_2017_02.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"thermophile\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Thermophile<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">grows best in hot<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">springs and vents<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Optimum<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">roughly 45 to 80<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">degrees C<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">An organism that thrives at high temperatures, such as in hot springs.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>嗜热菌<\/b>：在温泉等高温环境中茁壮生长的生物。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">thermo = heat, as in thermometer.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">thermo = 热。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does a thermophile love?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Heat.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.methanogen", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">meth<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">AN<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">gen<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"methanogen\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: methanogen\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"methanogen\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"46.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Hydrogen<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">+ CO2<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">(no<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"80.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">oxygen)<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"58.2\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Methanogen<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"67.4\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">(archaeon)<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Methane<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">gas<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">An archaeon that makes methane gas and cannot live where there is oxygen.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>产甲烷菌<\/b>：能产生甲烷气体的古菌，不能在有氧的环境生活。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">methane + -gen (producer).<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">methane + -gen（产生者）。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What gas does a methanogen make?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Methane.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.biofilm", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">BI<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">film<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"biofilm\" data-audio=\"audio/biofilm.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: biofilm\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u3-biofilm.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"538\" alt=\"A biofilm of Staphylococcus bacteria under an electron microscope: cells stuck together in a slimy layer.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A biofilm of Staphylococcus bacteria under an electron microscope: cells stuck together in a slimy layer.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">电子显微镜下的葡萄球菌生物膜：细胞被黏液层粘在一起。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: CDC / Rodney M. Donlan, Janice Carr (PHIL 7488) · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Staphylococcus_aureus_biofilm_01.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"biofilm\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"82\" width=\"180\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f7\"/><path d=\"M10 60 Q55 50 100 60 Q145 70 190 60 L190 82 L10 82 Z\" class=\"f6 d\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"72\" r=\"4\" class=\"f3\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"72\" r=\"4\" class=\"f4\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"72\" r=\"4\" class=\"f3\"/><circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"68\" r=\"4\" class=\"f5\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">microbes + slime on a surface<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">biofilm<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A thin, slimy layer of microbes stuck to a surface, such as plaque on teeth.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>生物膜<\/b>：附着在表面的一层黏滑的微生物，如牙菌斑。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">bio = life, film = thin layer.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">bio = 生命，film = 薄层。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Give an example of a biofilm.<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Dental plaque, or the slime on a river stone.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "cu.q.u3.t.mutualism", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A relationship in which both species benefit.”<\/i>", "opts": ["spirillum", "nitrogen fixation", "mutualism", "host cell"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>mutualism<\/b>: A relationship in which both species benefit. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">互利共生<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.microbiome", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“The community of microbes that live on and inside a body.”<\/i>", "opts": ["nitrogen fixation", "methanogen", "microbiome", "capsule"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>microbiome<\/b>: The community of microbes that live on and inside a body. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">微生物组<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.extremophile", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“An organism, often an archaeon, that thrives in extreme conditions such as heat, salt or acid.”<\/i>", "opts": ["capsid", "vaccine", "extremophile", "cyanobacteria"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>extremophile<\/b>: An organism, often an archaeon, that thrives in extreme conditions such as heat, salt or acid. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">极端微生物<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.halophile", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“An organism that lives in very salty places.”<\/i>", "opts": ["aerobic", "nitrogen fixation", "halophile", "flagellum"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>halophile<\/b>: An organism that lives in very salty places. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">嗜盐菌<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.thermophile", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“An organism that thrives at high temperatures, such as in hot springs.”<\/i>", "opts": ["thermophile", "halophile", "extremophile", "aerobic"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>thermophile<\/b>: An organism that thrives at high temperatures, such as in hot springs. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">嗜热菌<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.methanogen", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“An archaeon that makes methane gas and cannot live where there is oxygen.”<\/i>", "opts": ["capsule", "obligate parasite", "conjugation", "methanogen"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>methanogen<\/b>: An archaeon that makes methane gas and cannot live where there is oxygen. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">产甲烷菌<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.biofilm", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A thin, slimy layer of microbes stuck to a surface, such as plaque on teeth.”<\/i>", "opts": ["pilus", "aerobic", "methanogen", "biofilm"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>biofilm<\/b>: A thin, slimy layer of microbes stuck to a surface, such as plaque on teeth. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">生物膜<\/span>", "whys": null}]}